  "terminal": {
    "status": "REQUEST_COMPLETED",
    "payload": {
      "rootMessageId": "request-2c021662-5861-4b34-b509-c9c579c7dad8",
      "requestId": "request-2c021662-5861-4b34-b509-c9c579c7dad8",
      "runId": "run-ad17d214-d0f3-46b8-a57d-059ccd53518a",
      "requestContextId": "context-bf65310f-9399-4e22-b62b-b5f49402c898",
      "status": "COMPLETED",
      "content": "Done. **13 stations** experienced flooding during April 1–7, 2025, and the results are in `workspace/output/flood_results.csv`:\n\n| station_id | flood_days |\n|---|---|\n| 04101800 | 5 |\n| 04124000 | 5 |\n| 04097500 | 4 |\n| 04112500 | 3 |\n| 04112850 | 3 |\n| 04151500 | 3 |\n| 04164500 | 3 |\n| 04115000 | 2 |\n| 04142000 | 2 |\n| 04166500 | 2 |\n| 04117500 | 1 |\n| 04148140 | 1 |\n| 04164000 | 1 |\n\n**Method:**\n1. Read 79 station IDs from `workspace/data/michigan_stations.txt`.\n2. Downloaded the NWS bulk gauge report and matched all 79 stations to their `flood stage` thresholds.\n3. Downloaded USGS instantaneous gage height (parameter 00065, 15-min intervals) for each station via `dataretrieval.nwis.get_iv()` — all 79 stations returned data.\n4. Aggregated to daily maximum and counted days where `daily_max >= flood_stage`, restricted to April 1–7 (I verified that USGS's inclusive `endDT` returned April 8 data, but excluding it changed no counts).\n5. Kept only stations with ≥1 flood day, sorted by flood days descending.\n\nSpot-checked 04101800 (5 of 7 days at 8.5–9.3 ft vs. 8.0 ft flood stage) and 04117500 (only April 6 at 7.01 ft vs. 7.0 ft stage) — both match the output.",
      "text": "Done. **13 stations** experienced flooding during April 1–7, 2025, and the results are in `workspace/output/flood_results.csv`:\n\n| station_id | flood_days |\n|---|---|\n| 04101800 | 5 |\n| 04124000 | 5 |\n| 04097500 | 4 |\n| 04112500 | 3 |\n| 04112850 | 3 |\n| 04151500 | 3 |\n| 04164500 | 3 |\n| 04115000 | 2 |\n| 04142000 | 2 |\n| 04166500 | 2 |\n| 04117500 | 1 |\n| 04148140 | 1 |\n| 04164000 | 1 |\n\n**Method:**\n1. Read 79 station IDs from `workspace/data/michigan_stations.txt`.\n2. Downloaded the NWS bulk gauge report and matched all 79 stations to their `flood stage` thresholds.\n3. Downloaded USGS instantaneous gage height (parameter 00065, 15-min intervals) for each station via `dataretrieval.nwis.get_iv()` — all 79 stations returned data.\n4. Aggregated to daily maximum and counted days where `daily_max >= flood_stage`, restricted to April 1–7 (I verified that USGS's inclusive `endDT` returned April 8 data, but excluding it changed no counts).\n5. Kept only stations with ≥1 flood day, sorted by flood days descending.\n\nSpot-checked 04101800 (5 of 7 days at 8.5–9.3 ft vs. 8.0 ft flood stage) and 04117500 (only April 6 at 7.01 ft vs. 7.0 ft stage) — both match the output.",
      "contentType": "PLAIN_TEXT",
